---
import CourseSlideLayout from '../../../layouts/CourseSlideLayout.astro';
import LessonDeckChrome from '../../../components/lessons/LessonDeckChrome.astro';
import '../../../styles/q-methodology.css';
import { withBase } from '../../../utils/paths';
const title = 'Q methodology · Postgraduate workshop · April Jiawei Zhang';
const description = 'A 15 minute introduction to Q methodology, with a Q sorting activity and practical guidance for postgraduate research. October 2026.';
const courseHref = withBase('/teaching/training/');
---
<CourseSlideLayout {title} {description} lessonDeck>
  <section class="q-access" aria-labelledby="access-title" data-q-access>
    <p>Postgraduate workshop · October 2026</p>
    <h1 id="access-title">Q methodology</h1>
    <p>A 15 minute introduction to studying shared viewpoints.</p>
    <form data-q-access-form>
      <label for="q-access-code">Workshop access code</label>
      <div><input id="q-access-code" name="code" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" required aria-describedby="q-access-feedback" /><button type="submit">Open slides</button></div>
      <p id="q-access-feedback" role="status" data-q-access-feedback></p>
    </form>
    <a href={courseHref}>Back to training</a>
    <noscript>Enable JavaScript to enter the workshop and use the slides.</noscript>
  </section>
  <div data-q-workshop hidden>
    <LessonDeckChrome {courseHref} courseLabel="training materials" lessonTitle="Q methodology" />
    <main class="deck q-deck" aria-label="Q methodology slide deck">
<section class="slide is-active" data-title="Q methodology" aria-hidden="false"><div class="slide-inner title-slide">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Postgraduate workshop · October 2026</span></header>
<div class="title-rule"></div>
<div data-language="en"><h1>Q methodology</h1><p class="lead">Understanding shared viewpoints</p><p class="q-cover-meta">April Jiawei Zhang<br />A 15 minute introduction</p><p>What does Q study? How do we design, sort and interpret a Q study?</p><div class="q-cover-sort" aria-label="Example sorting grid with one, two, three, two and one spaces"><div><b>−2</b><span></span></div><div><b>−1</b><span></span><span></span></div><div><b>0</b><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><div><b>+1</b><span></span><span></span></div><div><b>+2</b><span></span></div></div></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h1>Q 方法</h1><p class="lead">理解共同觀點</p><p class="q-cover-meta">April Jiawei Zhang 張家維<br />15分鐘入門</p><p>Q研究甚麼？如何設計、排序及詮釋一項Q研究？</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="What Q studies" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Understanding Q</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>What different viewpoints exist?</h2><p class="lead">Q systematically studies <strong>subjectivity</strong>: how people understand and evaluate an issue from their own point of view.</p><div class="q-two"><article><h3>Participants express a viewpoint</h3><p>Each person ranks the same statements in relation to one another.</p></article><article><h3>Researchers compare whole sorts</h3><p>Factor analysis identifies shared patterns. Participants’ explanations help interpret their meaning.</p></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">A typical purposive Q study describes viewpoints. It cannot estimate what percentage of a population holds each view or establish causal effects.</p><p class="source-note">Brown (1993); Watts &amp; Stenner (2005)</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>有哪些不同觀點？</h2><p class="lead">Q有系統地研究<strong>主觀性</strong>：人們如何從自身角度理解及評價一個議題。</p><div class="q-two"><article><h3>參與者表達觀點</h3><p>每人把同一組陳述作相對排序。</p></article><article><h3>研究者比較整份排序</h3><p>因素分析辨識共同模式，再結合參與者的解釋理解其意義。</p></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">典型的立意取樣Q研究描述觀點，不能估計各觀點在母群體中的比例，也不能確立因果關係。</p><p class="source-note">Brown（1993）；Watts與Stenner（2005）</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="A question suited to Q" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Study design</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Music, identity and English learning</h2><blockquote>How do fans understand their identity and English learning when they engage with English-language singers and lyrics?</blockquote><p>Seek contrasting experiences: deliberate lyric study, listening for pleasure, cultural belonging and connection with other fans.</p><ol class="q-process"><li>Focus the question</li><li>Map the concourse</li><li>Select the Q set</li><li>Recruit the P set</li><li>Sort and interview</li><li>Analyse and interpret</li></ol><p class="q-takeaway">The research question concerns ways of making sense of an experience.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>音樂、身份與英語學習</h2><blockquote>歌迷接觸英語歌手及歌詞時，如何理解自身身份與英語學習？</blockquote><p>尋找不同經驗：刻意研習歌詞、以聆聽為樂、文化歸屬，以及與其他歌迷的連繫。</p><ol class="q-process"><li>聚焦研究問題</li><li>整理論述總體</li><li>選取Q陳述集</li><li>招募P參與者集</li><li>排序及訪談</li><li>分析與詮釋</li></ol><p class="q-takeaway">研究問題關注人們如何理解一段經驗。</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="From the concourse to the Q set" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Study design</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Give different views room to appear</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>Concourse</h3><p>The wider range of things people say about the topic.</p><p>Gather interviews, fan discussions and literature. Keep statement sources and seek less visible views.</p></article><article><h3>Q set</h3><p>The smaller collection everyone sorts.</p><p>Cover the range of meanings. Remove repetition, leading wording and statements with several ideas.</p></article></div><div class="q-example"><p><strong>Too much in one statement</strong><br />“Songs improve my English and make me feel like a global citizen.”</p><p><strong>Separate the ideas</strong><br />“I deliberately study lyrics to improve my English.”<br />“Following English-language singers makes me feel part of a global community.”</p></div><p class="q-takeaway">Pilot wording, missing perspectives and task burden with people similar to your participants.</p><p class="source-note">Watts &amp; Stenner (2005)</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>讓不同觀點有表達空間</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>論述總體 concourse</h3><p>人們圍繞議題所表達的廣泛看法。</p><p>蒐集訪談、歌迷討論及文獻。記錄陳述來源，尋找較少被聽見的觀點。</p></article><article><h3>Q陳述集 Q set</h3><p>所有參與者實際排序的較小陳述集合。</p><p>涵蓋不同意義，刪除重複、誘導性及同時包含多個想法的陳述。</p></article></div><div class="q-example"><p><strong>一項陳述包含過多想法</strong><br />「歌曲既改善我的英語，也讓我覺得自己是世界公民。」</p><p><strong>分開表達</strong><br />「我會刻意研習歌詞，以改善英語。」<br />「追隨英語歌手讓我覺得自己是全球社群的一分子。」</p></div><p class="q-takeaway">邀請與目標參與者相近的人試做，檢查措辭、遺漏觀點及任務負擔。</p><p class="source-note">Watts與Stenner（2005）</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Participants and instructions" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Study design</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Who should sort, and on what basis?</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>P set</h3><p>Recruit people with relevant, varied experiences and viewpoints.</p><p>For planning, you might consider 36 statements and 25–30 participants. These are illustrative choices, not universal rules.</p></article><article><h3>Condition of instruction</h3><p>Use the same clear sorting question for everyone.</p><blockquote>Thinking about your own experience with English-language music, rank these statements from most disagree to most agree.</blockquote></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">Justify the sample and grid, pilot the procedure, and arrange consent and secure data storage before collecting research data.</p><p class="source-note">van Exel &amp; de Graaf (2005); Watts &amp; Stenner (2005)</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>誰來排序？根據甚麼排序？</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>P參與者集 P set</h3><p>招募具相關但不同經驗及觀點的人。</p><p>規劃時可暫以36項陳述、25至30人作例子；這些只是示例，並非通用規則。</p></article><article><h3>排序指示 condition of instruction</h3><p>所有人使用同一個清楚的排序問題。</p><blockquote>根據你接觸英語音樂的自身經驗，把以下陳述從最不同意排至最同意。</blockquote></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">說明樣本及格網的理據，試行整個程序，並在研究資料收集前安排知情同意與安全儲存。</p><p class="source-note">van Exel與de Graaf（2005）；Watts與Stenner（2005）</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Try a Q sort" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity · 3 minutes including discussion</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Try a nine-statement Q sort</h2><p class="q-sort-instruction">Think about your own experience with English-language music. Read all nine statements, then assign each a position.</p><div class="q-sort-workspace"><div class="q-statements"><label class="q-statement"><b>1</b><span>Following English-language singers makes me feel part of a global community.</span><select data-sort-id="1" aria-label="Rank statement 1"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>2</b><span>Sharing songs helps me connect with other fans.</span><select data-sort-id="2" aria-label="Rank statement 2"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>3</b><span>Understanding a song’s cultural context matters to me.</span><select data-sort-id="3" aria-label="Rank statement 3"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>4</b><span>Enjoying the music is my main reason for listening.</span><select data-sort-id="4" aria-label="Rank statement 4"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>5</b><span>My own cultural identity remains central when I enjoy English songs.</span><select data-sort-id="5" aria-label="Rank statement 5"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>6</b><span>I deliberately study lyrics to improve my English.</span><select data-sort-id="6" aria-label="Rank statement 6"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>7</b><span>I feel confident joining conversations in English about music.</span><select data-sort-id="7" aria-label="Rank statement 7"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>8</b><span>I see myself as an English learner when I listen.</span><select data-sort-id="8" aria-label="Rank statement 8"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>9</b><span>I prefer translated lyrics to working out the English myself.</span><select data-sort-id="9" aria-label="Rank statement 9"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label></div><div class="q-sort-board"><div class="q-rank-ends"><span>Most disagree</span><span>Most agree</span></div><div class="q-rank-grid"><div class="q-rank-column"><b>-2</b><small data-rank-count="-2">0 / 1</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="-2" aria-label="Statements at -2"><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>-1</b><small data-rank-count="-1">0 / 2</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="-1" aria-label="Statements at -1"><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>0</b><small data-rank-count="0">0 / 3</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="0" aria-label="Statements at 0"><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>+1</b><small data-rank-count="1">0 / 2</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="1" aria-label="Statements at +1"><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>+2</b><small data-rank-count="2">0 / 1</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="2" aria-label="Statements at +2"><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div></div><p class="q-sort-hint">Use the spaces in the 1–2–3–2–1 pattern. Numbers on the grid refer to the statements on the left.</p><div class="q-actions"><button type="button" data-check-sort>Check my sort</button><button type="button" class="secondary" data-reset-sort>Reset sort</button></div><p class="q-feedback" data-sort-feedback role="status"></p><p class="source-note">Teaching example only. Choices stay in this browser and are not submitted. If you have no relevant experience, observe a partner.</p></div></div></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>試做九項陳述的Q排序</h2><p class="q-sort-instruction">根據你接觸英語音樂的自身經驗，讀完九項陳述，再為每項選擇位置。</p><div class="q-sort-workspace"><div class="q-statements"><label class="q-statement"><b>1</b><span>追隨英語歌手讓我覺得自己是全球社群的一分子。</span><select data-sort-id="1" aria-label="排序陳述 1"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>2</b><span>分享歌曲有助我與其他歌迷建立連繫。</span><select data-sort-id="2" aria-label="排序陳述 2"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>3</b><span>理解歌曲的文化背景對我很重要。</span><select data-sort-id="3" aria-label="排序陳述 3"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>4</b><span>享受音樂是我聆聽的主要原因。</span><select data-sort-id="4" aria-label="排序陳述 4"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>5</b><span>欣賞英語歌曲時，我自身的文化身份仍處於核心位置。</span><select data-sort-id="5" aria-label="排序陳述 5"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>6</b><span>我會刻意研習歌詞，以改善英語。</span><select data-sort-id="6" aria-label="排序陳述 6"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>7</b><span>我有信心參與以英語談論音樂的對話。</span><select data-sort-id="7" aria-label="排序陳述 7"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>8</b><span>聆聽時，我視自己為英語學習者。</span><select data-sort-id="8" aria-label="排序陳述 8"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label><label class="q-statement"><b>9</b><span>我較喜歡閱讀翻譯歌詞，而非自行理解英文。</span><select data-sort-id="9" aria-label="排序陳述 9"><option value="">選擇</option><option value="-2">-2</option><option value="-1">-1</option><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">+1</option><option value="2">+2</option></select></label></div><div class="q-sort-board"><div class="q-rank-ends"><span>最不同意</span><span>最同意</span></div><div class="q-rank-grid"><div class="q-rank-column"><b>-2</b><small data-rank-count="-2">0 / 1</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="-2" aria-label="陳述位置 -2"><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>-1</b><small data-rank-count="-1">0 / 2</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="-1" aria-label="陳述位置 -1"><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>0</b><small data-rank-count="0">0 / 3</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="0" aria-label="陳述位置 0"><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>+1</b><small data-rank-count="1">0 / 2</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="1" aria-label="陳述位置 +1"><span class="q-slot">—</span><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div><div class="q-rank-column"><b>+2</b><small data-rank-count="2">0 / 1</small><div class="q-slots" data-rank-slots="2" aria-label="陳述位置 +2"><span class="q-slot">—</span></div></div></div><p class="q-sort-hint">依照1–2–3–2–1的格數分配。格網中的數字對應左方的陳述編號。</p><div class="q-actions"><button type="button" data-check-sort>檢查排序</button><button type="button" class="secondary" data-reset-sort>重設排序</button></div><p class="q-feedback" data-sort-feedback role="status"></p><p class="source-note">僅供教學。選擇只保留於此瀏覽器，並不提交；沒有相關經驗者可觀察同伴。</p></div></div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Ask about the sorting decisions" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">After sorting</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>What did those positions mean to you?</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>Your +2 statement</h3><p data-endpoint="2">Complete the sort to see your statement here.</p><p>Why does this statement best express your view?</p></article><article><h3>Your −2 statement</h3><p data-endpoint="-2">Complete the sort to see your statement here.</p><p>Why does this statement fit your view least well?</p></article></div><p class="lead small">Which choice was difficult? What did the middle mean? Was an important view missing?</p><p class="q-takeaway">Positions are relative within a person’s sort. A negative score can mean less agreement than with the other statements; zero can reflect ambivalence or lower salience.</p><p>The grid structures comparison. Its shape does not show that people’s opinions are normally distributed.</p><p class="source-note">van Exel &amp; de Graaf (2005)</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>這些位置對你有甚麼意義？</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>你的+2陳述</h3><p data-endpoint="2">完成排序後，這裡會顯示你的陳述。</p><p>為甚麼這項最能表達你的觀點？</p></article><article><h3>你的−2陳述</h3><p data-endpoint="-2">完成排序後，這裡會顯示你的陳述。</p><p>為甚麼這項與你的觀點最不相符？</p></article></div><p class="lead small">哪項選擇最困難？中間位置代表甚麼？有沒有遺漏重要觀點？</p><p class="q-takeaway">位置在每人的排序內具有相對意義。負分可表示相較其他陳述較不同意；零分可反映矛盾感受或較低的關注程度。</p><p>格網協助比較，其形狀並不表示人們的意見服從常態分布。</p><p class="source-note">van Exel與de Graaf（2005）</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Record the complete sort" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Analysis</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Keep every statement’s position</h2><p class="lead small">Save the final layout and the post-sort explanation. Use participant codes and stable statement identifiers.</p><table class="q-data-table"><caption>One hypothetical sort in statement order</caption><thead><tr><th scope="row">Statement</th><th scope="col">1</th><th scope="col">2</th><th scope="col">3</th><th scope="col">4</th><th scope="col">5</th><th scope="col">6</th><th scope="col">7</th><th scope="col">8</th><th scope="col">9</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Score</th><td>+2</td><td>+1</td><td>0</td><td>−2</td><td>−1</td><td>+1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>−1</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="q-two"><article><h3>Check the record</h3><p>Every statement appears once. Scores match the grid. Entries match the saved layout.</p></article><article><h3>Compare complete Q-sorts</h3><p>Correlate each person’s whole sorting pattern with every other person’s pattern.</p></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">The key comparison is between Q-sorts, rather than between questionnaire items.</p><p class="source-note">Zabala (2014). Check the required row and column orientation before importing data.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>保留每項陳述的位置</h2><p class="lead small">保存最終格網及排序後的解釋。使用參與者代號及固定的陳述編號。</p><p class="q-array">陳述1至9的示例分數<br />+2, +1, 0, −2, −1, +1, 0, 0, −1</p><div class="q-two"><article><h3>核對記錄</h3><p>每項陳述出現一次，分數符合格網，輸入與已保存的排序一致。</p></article><article><h3>比較完整Q排序</h3><p>計算每人的整份排序與其他人的整份排序之間的相關。</p></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">關鍵是比較不同Q排序，而非問卷題項之間的相關。</p><p class="source-note">Zabala（2014）。匯入資料前核對軟件要求的列與欄方向。</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="From correlations to factors" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Analysis</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Identify shared patterns, then interpret them</h2><ol class="q-analysis"><li><strong>Extract and rotate</strong><span>Centroid factor analysis or principal components analysis; varimax or justified judgemental rotation.</span></li><li><strong>Compare candidate solutions</strong><span>Consider statistical evidence, defining sorts and interpretability together.</span></li><li><strong>Identify defining sorts</strong><span>Loadings show each sort’s relationship with a factor. State the flagging criteria.</span></li><li><strong>Construct factor arrays</strong><span>Combine defining sorts into an idealised ranking for each shared viewpoint.</span></li></ol><p class="q-takeaway">A sort may relate to several factors or define none. Avoid forcing every participant into one group.</p><p class="source-note">Zabala (2014). Ken-Q Analysis and KADE can support these steps; software does not choose the interpretation for you.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>辨識共同模式，再詮釋其意義</h2><ol class="q-analysis"><li><strong>抽取及轉軸</strong><span>重心因素分析或主成分分析；最大變異轉軸或有理據的判斷轉軸。</span></li><li><strong>比較候選方案</strong><span>綜合考慮統計證據、界定排序及可詮釋性。</span></li><li><strong>辨識界定排序</strong><span>負荷量顯示排序與因素的關係，需說明標記準則。</span></li><li><strong>建立因素排序陣列</strong><span>綜合界定排序，形成每個共同觀點的理想化排序。</span></li></ol><p class="q-takeaway">一份排序可能與多個因素有關，也可能未界定任何因素；避免強迫每人只歸入一組。</p><p class="source-note">Zabala（2014）。Ken-Q Analysis及KADE可支援這些步驟，但軟件不能代替研究者詮釋。</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Reading a factor array" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Interpretation</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>What does the whole pattern suggest?</h2><p>Hypothetical excerpts from two factor arrays. These are teaching illustrations, not study findings.</p><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Statement</th><th scope="col">Connection through music</th><th scope="col">Enjoyment comes first</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1. Global community</th><td>+2</td><td>−1</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4. Enjoyment as the main reason</th><td>−2</td><td>+2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6. Deliberate lyric study</th><td>+1</td><td>−2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7. Confidence discussing music</th><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="lead small">One pattern combines connection with language study. The other prioritises enjoyment and places deliberate study much lower.</p><p class="q-takeaway">Treat these as starting interpretations. Read every placement and participants’ explanations before naming the viewpoint.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>整體模式意味著甚麼？</h2><p>兩個因素排序陣列的假設片段，僅為教學示例，並非研究結果。</p><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">陳述</th><th scope="col">透過音樂建立連繫</th><th scope="col">享受優先</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1. 全球社群</th><td>+2</td><td>−1</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4. 主要為享受而聆聽</th><td>−2</td><td>+2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6. 刻意研習歌詞</th><td>+1</td><td>−2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7. 談論音樂的信心</th><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="lead small">一個模式結合社群連繫與語言學習；另一個優先重視享受，刻意研習則排得較低。</p><p class="q-takeaway">這只是初步詮釋。為觀點命名前，需檢視所有位置及參與者的解釋。</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Evidence for an interpretation" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Interpretation</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Support the viewpoint with evidence</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>Distinguishing statements</h3><p>Factor scores differ statistically under the chosen test. Different displayed ranks alone do not establish significance.</p></article><article><h3>Consensus statements</h3><p>No statistically significant differences across retained factors at the stated threshold. Consensus can concern agreement, disagreement or the middle.</p></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">Use the full array, tested factor differences and interview explanations. Seek evidence that complicates your first interpretation.</p><p>Report the statement selection, recruitment, grid and instructions, analytical decisions, loadings and arrays. Explain what perspectives your design may have missed.</p><p class="source-note">Brown (1993); Zabala (2014). A factor label describes a viewpoint, not a permanent personality type.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>以證據支持觀點詮釋</h2><div class="q-two"><article><h3>區辨陳述</h3><p>因素分數在所選檢定下有統計顯著差異；顯示的排序位置不同，本身不足以證明顯著性。</p></article><article><h3>共識陳述</h3><p>在所報告的門檻下，各保留因素之間沒有統計顯著差異。共識可涉及同意、不同意或中間位置。</p></article></div><p class="q-takeaway">結合完整陣列、經檢定的因素差異及訪談解釋，並尋找使初步詮釋更複雜的證據。</p><p>報告陳述選取、招募、格網與指示、分析決策、負荷量及排序陣列，也說明研究設計可能遺漏哪些觀點。</p><p class="source-note">Brown（1993）；Zabala（2014）。因素標籤描述觀點，而非固定人格類型。</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Check your understanding" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Understanding check</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Three questions before you leave</h2><div class="q-questions"><details><summary>Can this purposive Q study tell us the percentage of all postgraduates who share a viewpoint?</summary><p>No. Estimating prevalence requires an appropriate separate sampling and measurement design.</p></details><details><summary>What gets correlated in Q analysis?</summary><p>Participants’ complete Q-sorts.</p></details><details><summary>What evidence supports naming a factor?</summary><p>The whole factor array, its differences from other factors, and relevant participants’ explanations.</p></details></div><p class="q-takeaway">Explain your answer to a partner before opening each response.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>離開前的三個問題</h2><div class="q-questions"><details><summary>這項立意取樣Q研究能告訴我們全體研究生中有多少比例持某觀點嗎？</summary><p>不能。估計普遍程度需要另設合適的抽樣及測量設計。</p></details><details><summary>Q分析計算甚麼之間的相關？</summary><p>各參與者的完整Q排序。</p></details><details><summary>為因素命名需要甚麼證據？</summary><p>完整因素陣列、與其他因素的差異，以及相關參與者的解釋。</p></details></div><p class="q-takeaway">先向同伴解釋，再打開各題答案。</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Your first Q study" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Next steps</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Begin with your research question</h2><label class="q-write">A possible Q research question<textarea data-plan="question" rows="2" placeholder="What different viewpoints exist about…?"></textarea></label><label class="q-write">Two contrasting experiences to seek when recruiting<textarea data-plan="participants" rows="2" placeholder="Who might see this issue differently, and why?"></textarea></label><p class="source-note" data-plan-status>Notes stay in this browser and are not submitted.</p><p>Before collecting data: map the concourse, justify the Q set and P set, pilot the task, and plan consent and data protection.</p><p class="q-takeaway">For a dissertation, follow this introduction with methodological reading and supervised analysis practice.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>從自己的研究問題開始</h2><label class="q-write">一個可能的Q研究問題<textarea data-plan="question" rows="2" placeholder="圍繞某議題，存在哪些不同觀點？"></textarea></label><label class="q-write">招募時希望尋找的兩種不同經驗<textarea data-plan="participants" rows="2" placeholder="誰可能有不同看法？為甚麼？"></textarea></label><p class="source-note" data-plan-status>筆記只保留於此瀏覽器，並不提交。</p><p>收集資料前：整理論述總體，論證Q陳述集與P參與者集，試行任務，並規劃同意程序及資料保護。</p><p class="q-takeaway">用於學位論文前，需進一步閱讀方法文獻，並在指導下練習分析。</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-title="Reading and software" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
<header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Resources</span></header>

<div data-language="en"><h2>Continue with the method</h2><ul class="q-resources"><li><a href="https://ojs.library.okstate.edu/osu/index.php/osub/article/view/9020">Brown (1993). A primer on Q methodology.</a><span>Operant Subjectivity, 16(3/4), 91–138.</span></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1191/1478088705qp022oa">Watts &amp; Stenner (2005). Doing Q methodology.</a><span>Qualitative Research in Psychology, 2(1), 67–91.</span></li><li><a href="https://qmethod.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/qmethodologyasneakpreviewreferenceupdate.pdf">van Exel &amp; de Graaf (2005). Q methodology: A sneak preview.</a></li><li><a href="https://journal.r-project.org/articles/RJ-2014-032/">Zabala (2014). qmethod: A package to explore human perspectives.</a><span>The R Journal, 6(2), 163–173.</span></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.01360">Banasick (2019). KADE: A desktop application for Q methodology.</a><span>Journal of Open Source Software, 4(36), 1360.</span></li></ul><p><a href="https://shawnbanasick.github.io/ken-q-analysis/">Ken-Q Analysis</a> &nbsp; <a href="https://github.com/shawnbanasick/kade">KADE and documentation</a></p><p class="source-note">Adapted from the April 2025 Q methodology training and the 15-minute postgraduate teaching notes. All activity statements and factor examples are teaching illustrations.</p></div><div data-language="zh" lang="zh-Hant" hidden><h2>繼續學習Q方法</h2><ul class="q-resources"><li><a href="https://ojs.library.okstate.edu/osu/index.php/osub/article/view/9020">Brown (1993). A primer on Q methodology.</a><span>Operant Subjectivity, 16(3/4), 91–138.</span></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1191/1478088705qp022oa">Watts &amp; Stenner (2005). Doing Q methodology.</a><span>Qualitative Research in Psychology, 2(1), 67–91.</span></li><li><a href="https://qmethod.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/qmethodologyasneakpreviewreferenceupdate.pdf">van Exel &amp; de Graaf (2005). Q methodology: A sneak preview.</a></li><li><a href="https://journal.r-project.org/articles/RJ-2014-032/">Zabala (2014). qmethod: A package to explore human perspectives.</a><span>The R Journal, 6(2), 163–173.</span></li><li><a href="https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.01360">Banasick (2019). KADE: A desktop application for Q methodology.</a><span>Journal of Open Source Software, 4(36), 1360.</span></li></ul><p><a href="https://shawnbanasick.github.io/ken-q-analysis/">Ken-Q Analysis</a> &nbsp; <a href="https://github.com/shawnbanasick/kade">KADE and documentation</a></p><p class="source-note">根據2025年4月Q方法培訓及15分鐘研究生教學筆記改編。活動陳述與因素例子均僅供教學。</p></div>
</div></section>
